{"id": "x00979", "text": "- **Bouncing Pointer in Round-Robin:** Items are sorted DESC by duration (path ASC tie-break). Pointer starts at 0, direction +1. After assigning to `shards[ptr]`, `ptr += dir`. If `ptr >= shardCount`, `ptr = shardCount - 1` and `dir = -1`. If `ptr < 0`, `ptr = 0` and `dir = 1`. This naturally results in boundary shards getting two consecutive assignments."}
